{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793473480,"nonce":"+RHEhpTPUKr6h7GJI5F1L4wNBCo=","title":"Python embedding: no json.loads, and a host function cannot return a dict or list","message":"Reported by the dynASB embedding session (their git-bug 5b7d11d). The stdlib has json.dumps but no json.loads (b601fce lists json among the modules owed), and HostType offers Str/Int/Float/Bytes/Object/Dynamic, so a host handing a structured message to a handler has no way to return a dict or list; the only route seems to be a HostClass with accessor methods. An embedder needs either json.loads or a host return type that becomes a Python dict/list.","files":null}]}